== 3. Why Spearman and Pearson differ ========================== 
  RASSF9   Spearman rho = -0.120 (p=0.033) | Pearson on raw = -0.032 (p=0.570) | Pearson on log10 = -0.081 (p=0.150) 
  RASSF10  Spearman rho = -0.178 (p=0.001) | Pearson on raw = -0.122 (p=0.029) | Pearson on log10 = -0.217 (p=9.40e-05) 

  SBS7 spans three orders of magnitude (5 to 23,393). Pearson on the 
  raw scale is dominated by a handful of hypermutated tumours and is 
  therefore uninformative here; on the log scale it should align with 
  Spearman. Report Spearman as primary and the log-scale Pearson as 
  support; do not present the raw-scale Pearson as a contradiction. 

